From a6339f84ae9bba329630ab3740a4622011b27588 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niravkumar L Rabara <niravkumarlaxmidas.rabara@altera.com>
Date: Fri, 22 May 2026 15:33:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] platform/agilex5: route powerdown/standby through WFI

Agilex5 ATF rejects PSCI_CPU_SUSPEND for both StandBy and PowerDown
power state types with INVALID_PARAMS. Without action, Bao's
cpu_powerdown() and cpu_standby() helpers issue an SMC that fails
on every call, spamming the UART with

    BAO ERROR: PSCI cpu<N> power down failed with error 4294967294

and preventing OFF vCPUs from parking cleanly.

Use the upstream-supported plat-level fallbacks (already used by
s32g3, rpi4, zcu102, zcu104 and ultra96 for the same limitation):
when PLAT_PSCI_POWERDOWN_NOT_SUPPORTED / PLAT_PSCI_STANDBY_NOT_SUPPORTED
is defined, psci_power_down() / psci_standby() route through a plain
WFI and return PSCI_E_SUCCESS. cpu_arch_powerdown / cpu_arch_standby
then rewind the stack to cpu_powerdown_wakeup / cpu_standby_wakeup as
designed, so:

  - boot-time secondary vCPU bring-up via PSCI_CPU_ON works,
  - guest-issued PSCI_CPU_OFF parks the pCPU in WFI without SMC noise,
  - the next PSCI_CPU_ON IPI wakes WFI and re-enters vcpu_run with
    state == ON, reaching vcpu_arch_entry and ERETing into the guest's
    secondary entry point.

Signed-off-by: Niravkumar L Rabara <niravkumarlaxmidas.rabara@altera.com>
---
 src/platform/agilex5/inc/plat/psci.h | 19 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/platform/agilex5/inc/plat/psci.h b/src/platform/agilex5/inc/plat/psci.h
index 9e3aa31..ec738ab 100644
--- a/src/platform/agilex5/inc/plat/psci.h
+++ b/src/platform/agilex5/inc/plat/psci.h
@@ -7,8 +7,12 @@
 #define __PLAT_PSCI_H__
 
 /**
- * Agilex5 uses ATF (arm-trusted-firmware) with PSCI-0.2 via SMC.
- * Power state encoding follows ARM PSCI spec:
+ * Agilex5 uses ATF (arm-trusted-firmware) with PSCI-0.2 via SMC, but the ATF
+ * build for Agilex5 only supports PSCI_CPU_ON / PSCI_CPU_OFF for cold reset
+ * and rejects PSCI_CPU_SUSPEND for both StandBy and PowerDown power states
+ * with INVALID_PARAMS.
+ *
+ * Power state encoding still follows the ARM PSCI spec:
  *   - StateID in bits [27:0], StateType in bit [30]
  *   - PowerLevel in bits [25:24]
  */
@@ -19,6 +23,15 @@
 #define PSCI_STATE_TYPE_POWERDOWN       (1UL << 30)
 #define PSCI_STATE_TYPE_BIT             (1UL << 30)
 
-/* Agilex5 ATF supports both standby and powerdown via PSCI_SUSPEND */
+/*
+ * Route Bao's internal cpu_powerdown() / cpu_standby() through a plain WFI
+ * instead of PSCI_CPU_SUSPEND SMCs. This is the upstream-supported fallback
+ * already used by s32g3, rpi4, zcu102/104 and ultra96 for the same firmware
+ * limitation. cpu_arch_powerdown / cpu_arch_standby still rewind the stack
+ * to cpu_powerdown_wakeup / cpu_standby_wakeup on resume, so the Bao state
+ * machine (and PSCI_CPU_OFF -> PSCI_CPU_ON round-trips) keeps working.
+ */
+#define PLAT_PSCI_POWERDOWN_NOT_SUPPORTED 1
+#define PLAT_PSCI_STANDBY_NOT_SUPPORTED   1
 
 #endif /* __PLAT_PSCI_H__ */
-- 
